<title>CANADA: Monarch Developments buys two properties.</title>
<headline>Monarch Developments buys two properties.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monarch Development Corp on Friday said it completed the purchase of two undeveloped land sites in Canada and the United States.</p>
<p>The Toronto-based real estate developer said it acquired a parcel of vacant land zoned for a 61 unit condominium in Etobicoke, Ontario for about C$2.1 million.</p>
<p>The company's Florida-based Taylor Woodrow Communities joint venture also purchased 345 acres of undeveloped land in Florida for about US$2.3 million. The new site will add about 500 homesites to the joint venture's housing and land porfolio, the company said.</p>
<p>((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105, e-mail: jeffrey.hodgson@reuters.com))</p>
